TA-throttle
====

Collects CPU frequency state from /sys/devices/system/cpu (per-core current/min/max frequency, governor) and hardware thermal-throttle counters (package_throttle_count, mperf-based if present). Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype throttle:status) and throttle.* metrics to index=metrics (sourcetype throttle:metrics); alarm status when a thermal-throttle counter increases since the previous cycle.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * none - pure /sys reads (turbostat not required)
  * Fixed-frequency server CPUs (e.g. EPYC) expose fewer cpufreq sysfs knobs; throttle counters and core counts are still emitted
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="throttle:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="throttle:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="throttle.*" by host
  | mstats avg("throttle.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=throttle:status  (cpu_count, governors, min/max, throttle deltas)
Metrics: throttle.cpu_<n>_cur_freq_mhz, throttle.pkg_<n>_throttle_count, throttle.cpu_count
Dashboards: TA-Throttle > Throttle Overview / Throttle Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-throttle/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * cpufreq may be absent on fixed-frequency CPUs; cur_freq metrics are then omitted.
  * Throttle deltas use a state file under /var/tmp; first cycle after install has no baseline.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-throttle).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-throttle/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
